    "about": "z is the x-coordinate of ECDH(platformPrivateKey, keyPublicKey). sharedSecret = SHA-256(z). pinHash is the first 16 bytes of SHA-256(pinUtf8); pinHashEnc = AES-256-CBC(sharedSecret, all-zero IV, no padding) of it. The key sends its token encrypted the same way (tokenEnc). pinUvAuthParam = the first 16 bytes of HMAC-SHA-256(token, clientDataHash). requests are what the core sends (the command byte, then canonical CBOR), and answers what a key sends back (status 00, then CBOR). token16 is a CTAP 2.0 key's 16-byte token, with its own pinUvAuthParam16.",
